Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the Brim project.

## What was implemented:

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics by following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

### Created/Modified files:

1. **package.json** - Added `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1 as a dependency
2. **package-lock.json** - Updated lock file with the new dependency and its 587 transitive dependencies
3. **src/app/layout.tsx** - Added the Analytics component to the root layout:
   - Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
   - Placed `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body tag, after AppFooter

### Implementation details:

- Used Next.js App Router configuration (the project uses the app directory structure)
- The Analytics component is placed at the root layout level to track all pages
- Component is rendered at the end of the body for optimal loading performance
- Followed the exact pattern from the official Vercel documentation for Next.js 16.x

### Verification completed:

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ Linter ran with no errors
✅ All 909 tests passed (41 test files)
✅ TypeScript compilation succeeded
✅ Lock file properly updated

### Next steps:

Once deployed to Vercel, Web Analytics will automatically start collecting page views and other metrics. To view analytics data:
1. Deploy the project to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Vercel dashboard
3. Go to the project's Analytics section

No additional configuration is required - the analytics will work automatically in production on Vercel.
